2026-09-23T07:59:13.3938975Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3939201Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3939283Z     
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3939384Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3939466Z     
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3939574Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3939658Z     
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3939761Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3939851Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3939945Z             return x + 1
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3940021Z     
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3940102Z     
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3940198Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3940291Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3940373Z     
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3940452Z     
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3940543Z     To execute it::
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3940625Z     
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3940714Z         $ pytest
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3940882Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3940972Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3941054Z     
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3941152Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3941231Z     
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3941380Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3941673Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3941757Z     
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3941850Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3941947Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3942042Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3942131Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-23T07:59:13.3942212Z     
